  "description": "A transport-agnostic HTTP/3 connection for .NET: frame parsing, QPACK (static table and Huffman) and request dispatch, in pure managed C# with no native dependencies. Glyph3 does no I/O - it takes stream bytes in and hands stream bytes back - so it runs over System.Net.Quic, over io_uring, or over a pair of in-memory queues in a test. Buffered and streamed request bodies, and responses written through an IBufferWriter.",
